<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Märklin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Märklin is a German toy company founded in 1859 by Theodor Friedrich Wilhelm Märklin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goppingen">Göppingen</a>, Württemberg, at first making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> accessories for dolls' houses. In 1891 it introduced standard track gauges for clockwork model railways, and it became one of the world's best-known makers of model trains. The company is still based in Göppingen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marklin.jpg" alt="Märklin" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: qwesy qwesy · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A4rklin_Museum_in_G%C3%B6ppingen_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
